WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.047
Raw values are not always the form we want for analysis.

00:00:04.047 --> 00:00:08.197
Sometimes we need to convert them into meaningful categories.

00:00:08.197 --> 00:00:15.232
Map is useful when you have a dictionary that connects one value to another.

00:00:15.232 --> 00:00:20.372
Replace is useful when you want to substitute selected values.

00:00:20.372 --> 00:00:25.142
Cut is useful when you want to turn a numeric variable into ranges.

00:00:25.142 --> 00:00:31.737
In the example, we map Web and Email into an Online category, while Store becomes In person.

00:00:31.737 --> 00:00:37.900
We also use cut to classify order amounts as Small, Medium, or Large.

00:00:38.381 --> 00:00:41.913
These techniques are common in feature engineering and reporting.

00:00:41.913 --> 00:00:44.193
Age might become age groups.

00:00:44.193 --> 00:00:47.678
Income might become low, medium, and high.

00:00:47.678 --> 00:00:51.078
Product codes might become readable product names.

00:00:51.078 --> 00:00:53.813
Run the code and inspect the categories.

00:00:53.813 --> 00:00:58.833
Then change one of the bin boundaries and see which orders move into a different group.

00:00:58.833 --> 00:01:06.130
Always choose category boundaries carefully because those boundaries affect the interpretation of the analysis.
